    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1941505786477232313",
      "url": "https://x.com/followlastma/status/1941505786477232313",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/followlastma/status/1941505786477232313",
      "text": "[3:28PM] #TrafficUpdate #AlausaIkeja \n\nMobolaji Johnson Avenue, from the old Tollgate extending past the 7up gate to the Alausa intersection, is experiencing a smooth flow of vehicular traffic. Obafemi Awolowo Way is also characterized by good movement from the Barrack area, through Radio and Allen junctions, and towards Balogun; however, there is an observed increase in traffic density as vehicles approach the Ikeja underpass.\n\nA similar pattern is noted on Lateef Jakande Road, where traffic flows well from the Omole roundabout onwards through Wemco junction, Acme junction, Agidingbi, and Cadbury, with a noticeable increase in activity near the Coca-Cola junction, which is nonetheless moving. \n\nFurthermore, Aromire, connecting to Adeniyi Jones, is reporting appreciable traffic movement, with occasional traffic control interventions implemented as necessary to optimize flow. The Dr. Nurudeen Olowopopo stretch is also experiencing a smooth movement of vehicles. \n\nNo impediments to traffic have been reported within these areas, and our officers are actively stationed at key points to ensure the continued flow of traffic.\n\n#FollowLASTMA",
